There are many theories about the possible causes of schizophrenia. Studies suggest that it may be a combination of different factors that contribute to its development, including:  genetic influences, which means there is a greater chance of a person having the condition if a parent or sibling has it; 
  environmental influences, such as adverse experiences in early childhood;  
  changes in the way certain areas of the brain develop or function; and  hormone fluctuations that happen in the teen years.   It is important to note that these are all hypotheses and the exact cause is not always clear. Schizophrenia is treated with a combination of medication, talk therapy, self-management strategies, and lifestyle changes to help the patient learn to better cope with the condition and manage their symptoms.
